The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
if (mi != NULL) {
    _ncesmp = mi->n_elts;
    _icetsm = mi->elt_id;
}
_volume_mass_injection_get_field_arrays(f->id, &_itpsmp, &_smcelp);
```
Reason:
The improper handling of the conditional checks allowed the function `_volume_mass_injection_get_field_arrays` to be called even when `mi` was `NULL`, leading to the use of uninitialized parameters. This could result in a crash if the function attempted to access members of `mi` when it was not properly initialized.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
_volume_mass_injection_get_field_arrays(f->id, &_itpsmp, &_smcelp);
if (_ncesmp > 0)
    _volume_mass_injection_get_field_arrays(CS_F_(p)->id, NULL, &_gamma);
```
Reason:
The restructuring of the code ensures that the function calls are executed only when the conditions are met. By removing unnecessary braces and ensuring that `_volume_mass_injection_get_field_arrays` is called only when `mi` is not `NULL`, the risk of passing uninitialized parameters is mitigated, thus preventing the crash.

